  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 83,
  "title": "Psalms 83",
  "display_title": "Psalms 83",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 83,
  "sortOrder": 19083,
  "verseCount": 18,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from being a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Do unto them as unto the Midianites; as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the brook of Kison:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Which perished at Endor: they became as dung for the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:83:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "That men may know that thou, whose name alone is JEHOVAH, art the most high over all the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 83:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:83:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
